	(text "CC1/CC2: 5.1k each to GND (USB-C sink, 5 V only).\nFit R3/R4 for an ESP32-C6 module, R5/R6 (DNP) for a C3 module:\nthe two modules have USB on different pads (DECISIONS D15/D19)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 57.15 157.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "18897ba0-7acb-539b-b098-096d49c849db")
	)
	(text "RS485 (DIRECTION FROM TX)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 384.0139 217.045 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "41a93f23-db37-5cff-8c0f-caebbc1d9678")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM POWER: LOAD SHARING, 3.3 V LDO, SWITCHED RAILS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 634.748 69.725 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "48926603-e2c9-506c-95f5-8315e94d84b1")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so nothing back-powers sensors when the rail is off.\nFirmware must switch +3V3_SW on before ANY I2C traffic, including relay changes:\nthe TCA9534 (on always-on 3V3) holds its outputs meanwhile (D20). OLED shares the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 332.74 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "536e4fad-06eb-5848-8c90-e7a2328c0cf4")
	)
	(text "12 V INPUT, PROTECTION & 5 V BUCK"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 70.5317 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5dfeb3a2-0e78-52c2-b7c5-a981f4601770")
	)
	(text "TCA9534 pins start as inputs: the ULN2003's internal input resistors then hold\nevery relay off until firmware drives P0-P3 (D16). Address 0x20 (A0-A2 low).\nContacts are isolated from the board: wire loads to COM/NO/NC (D5, D24).\nContact copper for 5 A per channel at 1 oz; 12 V DC loads only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 487.68 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "664d8cb7-8f2c-5c53-bf0d-75674fc9eb84")
	)
	(text "USB-C INPUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 46.99 69.9873 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "67caffbb-fceb-5971-9b4f-038810c85524")
	)
	(text "Pads marked [C6]/[C3] differ between the two modules (D15, D18).\nEverything essential uses pads that work on both; BTN2 and GPIO_A/B work\nonly with a C6. SW2 is BOOT and BTN1 (IO9 strap). IO8/IO9 must be high at reset.\nC17/C18 close to module pin 3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 64.77 358.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "732443ba-5d71-5996-8e90-980254c9adfc")
	)
	(text "D2 blocks reverse polarity; D3 (SMAJ15A) clamps surges. 15 V max input.\nV12_SENSE = 12 V x 100k/660k: 2.27 V at 15 V, inside the ADC range (D23).\nAP63205: fixed 5 V out. L1/C6/C7 to be checked against the datasheet (D25)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 242.57 132.08 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8756e446-80a1-5c8f-9c67-58481ea6370b")
	)
	(text "PROG: I = 1200 / R. 4.7k = 255 mA; bridge JP1 (2.35k) = 510 mA (D12).\nTEMP: JP2 bridged disables the NTC input. For a cell NTC, cut JP2 and fit\nR11 + J3 with values from the TP4056 datasheet (D27).\nJ4 (JST-PH): pin 1 = cell -, pin 2 = cell +. JST-PH polarity is not standardised:\ncheck each cell before connecting (D28).\nProtection (DW01A + FS8205A) sits in the cell's negative lead: board GND is the pack's P-."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 485.14 77.47 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "90966913-07ec-5a37-983b-8f9c7e832eac")
	)
	(text "DI is tied low: the driver only ever sends 0, gated by TX through Q9.\nA 1 (and idle) is held by the 680R bias pair. Fine for Modbus at 9600 baud;\nmarginal with termination at both cable ends (D21). Bridge JP3 at a bus end.\nTransceiver, bias and pull-ups are on +3V3_SW, so RS485 is off with the rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 412.75 327.66 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "922ef50d-ec13-519a-8a00-b79b5e3883c1")
	)
	(text "LI-ION CHARGER & CELL PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 475.4831 69.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a9b143bc-da59-5edc-a63f-de070491fcd7")
	)
	(text "RELAY DRIVER & RELAYS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 47.8871 384.685 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c26ceca6-23fd-548d-9b46-03e9b21ee979")
	)
	(text "SENSOR PORTS: I2C, OLED, GPIO"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 266.0853 217.045 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c3fa418c-a434-513a-94ea-2c06539445d0")
	)
	(text "ESP32-C6 / C3 MODULE"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.0083 217.045 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e826539b-b7d7-5c5c-b7a5-61c2cf662c3e")
	)
	(text "D7 + Q2: with 5 V present VSYS comes through D7 and Q2 is off;\nwithout it Q2 turns on and the cell feeds VSYS. The charger never carries the load.\nVBAT_SENSE = VBAT / 2 (1M/1M, ~2 uA). RAIL_EN low (default, R21) = both rails off.\n+5V_SW only exists while USB or 12 V is present (no boost from the cell)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 654.05 166.37 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f5efe997-19b4-58e9-a3a0-7bf920f6af9d")
	)
